---
description: Keep NativeTavern UI/UX identical across Android, iOS, and desktop
alwaysApply: true
---

# Cross-platform UI/UX consistency

NativeTavern ships one product UI. Android, iOS, and desktop (macOS/Windows/Linux)
must look and behave the same unless a platform API forces a difference
(file pickers, permissions, Live2D host, system share sheets).

## Do

- Prefer shared widgets and theme tokens (`buildNativeTavernTheme`,
  `ChromeControls`, `SettingsSection` / `SettingsPageBody`, `spacedAppBarActions`)
  over per-platform layouts.
- Fix spacing, density, AppBar actions, FABs, and list chrome in the **theme**
  or a shared helper so every platform picks up the same change.
- Use `tooltip` / semantics when a control is icon-only so accessibility stays
  equivalent without visible labels.
- When a screen looks wrong on one platform, treat it as a product bug: make
  the shared UI match the intended design everywhere, do not paper over with
  `Platform.isX` branches.

## Don't

- Do not add `Platform.isAndroid` / `isIOS` / `isMacOS` (or width hacks that
  only target desktop) to diverge padding, icon size, FAB style, list density,
  or navigation chrome.
- Do not ship desktop-only “compact” chrome or mobile-only oversized rows for
  the same screen.
- Do not use `FloatingActionButton.extended` for primary create actions that
  should be a circular icon FAB on all platforms (e.g. home “new chat”).
- Do not leave AppBar action IconButtons flush to the trailing edge or packed
  with zero gap; use theme `actionsPadding` and `spacedAppBarActions`.

## Allowed platform differences

Capability and host integration only: pickers, permissions, Live2D/macOS
plugins, backup backends, window geometry. Those must not change the visual
hierarchy or control shapes of shared screens.
